!++
!  MODULE:		etc/mscphub.conf.example
!  IDENT:		X01-17
!
!  FACILITY:		MSCPHUB - MSCP disk server for OpenVMS nodes, over NISCA
!
!  ABSTRACT:		A sample configuration file of the server.  Copy it to mscphub.conf
!			next to it, change it, then start the server:
!
!			  systemctl start mscphub
!
!			One parameter per line, as on the command line.  A line that starts
!			with "!" is a comment.  "mscphub /HELP" describes every parameter.
!
!  AUTHOR:		StarLet Squad and Ruslan R. Laishev (AKA: BadAss SysMan)
!
!  CREATION DATE:	18-OCT-2026
!
!  MODIFICATION HISTORY:
!
!		22-OCT-2026	RRL	X01-16 : /HELP=/AUTHORIZE, the topic as it is named.
!		22-OCT-2026	RRL	X01-17 : /MODBUS.
!--
!
! The LAN interface the OpenVMS nodes are on.  The same LAN segment - a
! bridge, a VLAN, a switch - as their NISCA (PEDRIVER) adapters.
!
/INTERFACE=eth0
!
! Who the server is in the cluster: SCSNODE and SCSSYSTEMID of its own,
! used by no other node.
!
/NODE=MHUB
/SYSTEMID=65200
!
! The cluster: its group number and its password, as CLUSTER_CONFIG
! made them.  The password is the hash of CLUSTER_AUTHORIZE.DAT, see
! "mscphub /HELP=/AUTHORIZE" for how to read it on an OpenVMS node.
!
/GROUP=4242
/AUTHORIZE=0000000000000000
!
! The disks.  OpenVMS names them $<allocation class>$<name>: here
! $42$DKA100 and $42$DKA300.
!
/ALLOCLASS=42
/UNIT0=DKA100,/srv/mscphub/dka100.img
! /UNIT1=DKA200,/dev/sdb
! /UNIT2=DKA300,/srv/mscphub/AXPVMS083.iso,RO
!
! A diskless Alpha satellite the server loads by MOP: the address of the
! adapter it boots from, the unit of its system disk, its root there.
!
! /SATELLITE0=08-00-2B-E5-43-01,DKA100,SYS10
!
! When a WRITE is on the disk: DSYNC (the default, every WRITE), GROUP
! (one fdatasync for the writes that come together).
!
! /SYNC=GROUP
!
! The zone of the time the server tells the nodes: LOCAL (the default, the
! zone of this host), UTC, or an offset such as +03:00.
!
! /TIMEZONE=LOCAL
!
! When the server acknowledges the packets of a node alone: HOLD (the
! default, with its next packet, or after 4 packets or 20 ms), FLUSH (as
! soon as the frames that came in are taken).
!
! /ACK=HOLD
!
! The counters over Modbus/TCP, for a SCADA or a PLC panel: [address:]port.
! MHMON reads them on this computer without it.
!
! /MODBUS=502
